{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "tasks/an-agent-starts-its-work-in-the-background",
  "title": "An agent given work_in_background by setup_background calls it in its turn: the room's owner starts the task on the worker the host named and answers at once, the task's id, started, and where its result goes; the worker's result comes back to the agent as a turn of its own; a hand-back the setup does not know, and an agent the kit does not hold, are refused",
  "rules": [
    "§23.4",
    "§10.6.5",
    "§23.3 step 8"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/tasks/test_background_tasks.py::test_setup_declares_the_tool_on_the_agent, test_setup_refuses_an_unknown_hand_back, test_the_tool_starts_the_task_and_answers_at_once, test_the_task_runs_on_the_worker_the_host_named; core/mixins/background.py setup_background; tasks/background.py background_tool_server, BACKGROUND_TOOL_DEF. The tool's answer is Python's json.dumps of its members, in their order.",
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "sms",
        "type": "sms",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "helper",
        "type": "ai",
        "category": "intelligence",
        "on_event": [
          {
            "when": {
              "source_channel_id": "system",
              "type": "message"
            },
            "respond": [
              {
                "content": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "body": "Three tickets are open."
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "speaker",
        "type": "ai",
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "calls": [
                {
                  "id": "c1",
                  "name": "work_in_background",
                  "arguments": {
                    "task": "Count the open tickets."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "On it."
            },
            {
              "text": "Three tickets are open."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "room-1",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms"
          },
          {
            "channel_id": "speaker"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "call": "setup_background",
      "agent_id": "speaker",
      "hand_back": "shout",
      "expect": {
        "error": "invalid_argument"
      }
    },
    {
      "call": "setup_background",
      "agent_id": "nobody",
      "expect": {
        "error": "channel_not_registered"
      }
    },
    {
      "call": "setup_background",
      "agent_id": "speaker",
      "worker": "helper"
    },
    {
      "call": "process_inbound",
      "room_id": "room-1",
      "message": {
        "channel_id": "sms",
        "sender_id": "+15551234567",
        "content": {
          "type": "text",
          "body": "How many tickets are open?"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "idle": true
    }
  ],
  "expect": {
    "rooms": {
      "$r1": {
        "metadata": {
          "parent_room_id": "room-1",
          "task_agent_id": "helper",
          "task_status": "completed",
          "task_result": "Three tickets are open."
        }
      }
    },
    "models": {
      "speaker": [
        {
          "tool_results": []
        },
        {
          "tool_results": [
            {
              "tool_call_id": "c1",
              "content": {
                "$contains": "\"status\": \"started\", \"message\": \"The work runs in the background and its result comes back to speaker as a turn of its own when it is done. If this turn has not said so yet, say in one short sentence that it is under way; then end your turn, without saying it again.\"}"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "$any"
      ]
    }
  }
}
